# Top-level requirements of the one-file bundles: the input of
# build/requirements-bundle.txt (the lock). Refresh it with
# scripts/lock_bundle_deps.sh (the resolver runs in a container), never by
# hand.
#
# Every base dependency and every extra of pyproject.toml is listed here
# with its pyproject floor (tests/test_bundle_lock.py holds that), plus what
# only the build needs. The resolver picks the newest release that satisfies
# all of them; python -m security.dep_floor_audit --lock then checks every
# exact pin against OSV, malicious-package entries included.
#
# Linux builds both flavours in the AlmaLinux 9 builder image
# (Dockerfile.build); macOS and Windows build axross-slim in CI
# (.github/workflows/cross-platform.yml) from the same lock. What only
# axross-full (Linux) carries, or what slim excludes anyway, is marked
# linux-only, so the CI bundles carry the same packages as before the lock.

# --- base dependencies (pyproject [project].dependencies) ------------------
# Qt 6.11.2 fixes the SVG, QXmlStreamReader and QDom advisories 6.10.2 is
# subject to (wiki.qt.io/List_of_known_vulnerabilities_in_Qt_products);
# axross renders SVG thumbnails of untrusted files.
